01:15:33,060 --> 01:15:40,240
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: especially those who come home because of abuse, calamities, illegal recruitment or human trafficking.

1301
01:15:40,240 --> 01:15:48,180
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Number three, healthcare and education support not only for OFWs but also for their families here in the Philippines.

1302
01:15:48,540 --> 01:15:55,240
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: And finally, number four, proper monitoring to ensure that foreign employers strictly comply

1303
01:15:55,820 --> 01:15:56,640
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: with labor laws.

1304
01:15:56,660 --> 01:16:01,560
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Including establishment of accessible hotlines and digital platforms

1305
01:16:01,560 --> 01:16:05,520
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: where OFWs can immediately seek help in cases of abuse.

1306
01:16:06,280 --> 01:16:12,200
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Mr. Chair, we must remember that every peso allocated to and spent by the DMW and OWA

1307
01:16:12,200 --> 01:16:17,660
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: is an investment in the safety, dignity and future of our OFWs.

1308
01:16:18,580 --> 01:16:21,140
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: With that, I have some questions.

1309
01:16:21,140 --> 01:16:24,260
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, Senator Rafi.

1310
01:16:24,820 --> 01:16:26,540
Senator Joel Villanueva: We fully take note of your...

1311
01:16:26,660 --> 01:16:27,560
Senator Joel Villanueva: Four points.

1312
01:16:27,680 --> 01:16:36,520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Swift crisis response, safe repatriation and reintegration, support to OFWs and their families.

1313
01:16:36,520 --> 01:16:44,920
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I think one of the most important points you mentioned is the proper monitoring of our OFWs while they are working abroad.

1314
01:16:45,220 --> 01:16:47,980
Senator Joel Villanueva: You may proceed with your questions, Senator Rafi.

1315
01:16:48,060 --> 01:16:48,800
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

1316
01:16:49,380 --> 01:16:52,520
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Natataka ako, ba't binawasan ang budget ng DMW?

1317
01:16:53,300 --> 01:16:54,680
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Malit na nga, lalong niliitan.

1318
01:16:55,380 --> 01:16:56,000
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Anong nangyari?

1319
01:16:56,000 --> 01:16:57,460
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Anong nangyari sa DBM?

1320
01:16:57,620 --> 01:16:58,940
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Nasaan ang DBM natin dito?

1321
01:17:00,260 --> 01:17:02,200
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Siguro walang kamaganak ng OFW to.

1322
01:17:02,660 --> 01:17:03,740
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Bukta ng DBM na to.

1323
01:17:05,100 --> 01:17:10,660
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: But, yeah, 37.6 billion ang inyong proposed budget, Secretary Hans.

1324
01:17:12,320 --> 01:17:17,000
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: And yung Sagaan, 2026, na-approval 11.7.

1325
01:17:18,300 --> 01:17:22,560
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Mas lumit pa pagdating sa NEP, DBM approval 11.6.

1326
01:17:22,560 --> 01:17:23,640
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Ano pong binigay na reason?

1327
01:17:23,720 --> 01:17:25,560
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Meron ba binigay na reason ng DBM?

1328
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:32,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ah, Mr. Chair, ang sa pagkakaalam ko po, ah, mawalang gahalang sa DBM,

1329
01:17:32,620 --> 01:17:36,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: but ang pagkaalam ko, they were looking at previous historical utilization,

1330
01:17:37,080 --> 01:17:41,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kung saan medyo mababata-bata pa sa edad ang departamento namin.

1331
01:17:41,820 --> 01:17:45,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ah, 2023, 2024, ah, utilization.

1332
01:17:45,620 --> 01:17:49,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero definitely, Mr. Chair, ah, we hit our stride in 2025.

1333
01:17:49,660 --> 01:17:55,960
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ah, kung saan ang utilization namin, nearly 100%, including the continuing appropriation,

1334
01:17:56,000 --> 01:17:56,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: from 2024.

1335
01:17:57,260 --> 01:17:59,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And then, definitely, Mr. Chair, ubos po.

1336
01:17:59,800 --> 01:18:06,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ah, kami ni Admin PY, ah, ubos ang aming pondo, ah, dahil sa U.S.-Israel-Iran War.

1337
01:18:06,440 --> 01:18:11,720
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ah, but mukhang lagpas na po yata sa utilization review.

1338
01:18:12,240 --> 01:18:15,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Itong mga period na binabanggit ko.

1339
01:18:15,560 --> 01:18:21,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At, ah, the DBM, ah, of course, ah, they are our partners also, ah, Mr. Chair, Secretary Kim.

1340
01:18:21,080 --> 01:18:21,880
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Hindi ka nag-appeal.

1341
01:18:22,060 --> 01:18:22,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Opo.

1342
01:18:22,540 --> 01:18:22,760
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Sek.

1343
01:18:22,760 --> 01:18:25,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ah, nag-appeal din po, Mr. Senator.

1344
01:18:26,000 --> 01:18:33,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Senator, ah, ah, we, we did as much as we could, ah, but, but, ah, yes, we, we sought

1345
01:18:33,600 --> 01:18:38,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: reconsideration, ah, but Mr. Senator, ah, myself and Secretary Kim are one team under

1346
01:18:38,560 --> 01:18:39,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: the President.

1347
01:18:39,300 --> 01:18:43,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, ah, I will always, ah, submit to, to the DBM's determination.

1348
01:18:44,140 --> 01:18:49,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But, of course, we come, sumasumamo po kami sa inyo, ah, Mr. Senator, dahil, ah, 2 billion

1349
01:18:49,740 --> 01:18:55,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: po between Admin PY and ourselves, ah, 2 billion pong hinihingi namin, bali 4 billion pong karagdagan.

1350
01:18:56,260 --> 01:19:02,060
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Mr. Chair, ah, kasi, almost every day, sa program ako, sumanda sila sa Action Center,

1351
01:19:02,540 --> 01:19:06,800
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: manayin pupunta naman kapag-anak ng OFW natin na they wanted to be repatriated, yung kanilang

1352
01:19:06,800 --> 01:19:09,200
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: relatives doon na inabuso kadalasan.

1353
01:19:09,980 --> 01:19:14,040
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Ah, hindi maganda yung kalagayan at pagtrato at nakakaawa talaga.

1354
01:19:14,140 --> 01:19:19,520
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Eh, nakikita ko naman yung DMW natin at OFW, ayaw yung, yung OWA, eh, nagtatrabaho naman talaga

1355
01:19:19,520 --> 01:19:21,260
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: to ensure na sila'y mapabalik dito.

1356
01:19:21,940 --> 01:19:25,820
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: At, ah, malaking pakinabang talaga ng mga OFW sa dalawang nabanggit.

1357
01:19:26,000 --> 01:19:50,620
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Ito yung mga agency or department. The problem lang here is kulang sa budget ngayon sa nakikita ko. Paano silang makagalaw kung tali naman yung kanilang mga kamay when it comes to budget dahil imbis na i-consider ng DPM at pag-aralan yung kanilang proposed budget, pinutulan pa.

1358
01:19:50,620 --> 01:20:06,220
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Now, Mr. Chair, dito sa 2 billion na nirequest nila, 1 billion sa Action Fund, sa DMW ito, 1 billion sa MOOE, and then sa OWWA, 2 billion, 500 for Emergency Repatriation Fund. Hindi pa kayong pagbigyan ito?

1359
01:20:08,600 --> 01:20:19,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: Mr. Senator, if I will be asked about it, I am fully supporting it and with your help, we will fight for it in the budget deliberation.

1360
01:20:19,220 --> 01:20:40,000
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: So how do we go about na i-push natin ito? Ito sa mga tinatawag nating makabagong bayani at alam naman natin kahit na noong pampanahon ay nagkagewang-gewang na ekonomiya ng mundo, nagkaroon ng world crisis, lumulutang-lutang pa rin tayo dahil nandiyan po yung ating mga OFWs na nakapack up, nakasuporta sa atin through their remittances.

1361
01:20:40,400 --> 01:20:48,080
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Ngayon, kailangan nila natin tulong through the DMW and OWA. Siguro naman, we really need to support.

1362
01:20:49,220 --> 01:20:58,160
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: The DMW and OWA na sila nagkaalaga sa ating mga OFWs. So how do we go about pagdating sa budget deliberation? May ibigay itong 2 billion?

1363
01:20:58,160 --> 01:21:08,940
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, tama po kayo. Record high yung pinapadala ng OFWs na 39.62 billion US dollars in personal remittances.

1364
01:21:08,940 --> 01:21:19,200
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ang sa atin lang po ay alam nyo naman how budgeting works when you increase the budget of a particular agency or increase.

1365
01:21:19,220 --> 01:21:27,020
Senator Joel Villanueva: The budget of an item here, we have to find out saan natin na po pwedeng kuhanin.

1366
01:21:27,200 --> 01:21:38,680
Senator Joel Villanueva: Isa po kanina dun sa napag-usapan nga natin, isa sa nakita natin kanina, Senator Rafi, merong nilagyan ng pondo yung personal services pero wala namang item.

1367
01:21:38,680 --> 01:21:47,040
Senator Joel Villanueva: So mukhang hindi nila mapapakinabangan yung dinagdag na pondo dun sa OWA dahil wala namang item, wala namang plantilya.

1368
01:21:47,040 --> 01:21:57,760
Senator Joel Villanueva: So that's 200 million already, but according to our friends from OWA, kung malabas naman yung plantilya, kaya nilang punan ito.

1369
01:21:57,920 --> 01:22:14,620
Senator Joel Villanueva: So we'll find ways and of course with your help and the support of Senator Javis, our finance chair, he gave me assurance that he will join us later on today as we look into the budget of DMW and OWA.

1370
01:22:14,620 --> 01:22:16,840
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Okay, thank you. Dalawang tanong na lamang.

1371
01:22:17,040 --> 01:22:37,760
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Mr. Chair, Sec. Hans, doon po sa mga seafarers natin na ayaw maglayag dahil doon sa mga drone strikes, natakot sila, ayaw nilang pumalaot, ito mga tripulanting ito, anong tulong ang pwedeng maibigay sa mga ito?

1372
01:22:39,460 --> 01:22:46,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes po, ang bilang po natin, Mr. Senator, Mr. Chair, is 1,500 po.

1373
01:22:46,680 --> 01:22:55,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: In the last three years, na itinalaga natin yung issuance natin, pagkilala ng right to refuse sailing, 1,500 po ang nag-manifest.

1374
01:22:55,340 --> 01:23:05,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, Mr. Senator, nakalagay po doon sa 1,500, nakalagay po sa rules natin on right to refuse sailing, they should not be discriminated against.

1375
01:23:06,620 --> 01:23:16,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ang magandang balita po dito, the 1,500 who have been reported to us and affirmed by their respective license mining agencies, hindi naman po silang pinagbabawalan.

1376
01:23:16,020 --> 01:23:34,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, as far as we know, wala pong naapekto hang nag-exercise ng right to refuse sailing dahil marami naman pong rota ang mga shipping lines at they are just merely transferred from one voyage, one assignment to another.

1377
01:23:35,220 --> 01:23:44,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But having said that, yun pong mga umuuwi ay binibigyan po natin ng action fund benefit as they come home, Mr. Senator.

1378
01:23:46,020 --> 01:23:59,940
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Second, saan pa mas mga kamura tayo yung marami tayong tie-up sa mga different hotels partners natin kapag may mga dumarating ng mga OFWs before they are sent back to their homes in the provinces?

1379
01:24:00,620 --> 01:24:11,080
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: So, chine-check-in sila sa tulad ng kabayano, hotel and all other hotels versus kung tayo ay magtayo ng mga accommodation houses.

1380
01:24:11,540 --> 01:24:15,840
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Kasi paano kung puno yung hotel at that time dumating ng mga OFWs, marami sila, kunyari 20 eh.

1381
01:24:16,020 --> 01:24:17,960
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Wala na palang room na available.

1382
01:24:18,780 --> 01:24:28,920
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Kung tayo ay magtatayo ng sarili natin mga accommodation houses para sa mga repatriated OFWs papunta probinsya, which one sa tingin ninyo mas more practical?

1383
01:24:29,180 --> 01:24:32,260
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Yung mag-tie-up sa mga hotel o magpatayo tayo ng mga accommodation houses?

1384
01:24:32,260 --> 01:24:36,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ako pong tingin ko po dyan at ito lumabas na yung issue neto ng COVID.

1385
01:24:37,180 --> 01:24:43,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kung ang scale po ng repatriation is a global pandemic o a global conflict, global crisis,

1386
01:24:44,060 --> 01:24:45,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: kung saan libo o daang libo

1387
01:24:46,020 --> 01:24:50,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ang umuuwi, mainam po na yung private sector po ang mag-handle.

1388
01:24:50,760 --> 01:24:55,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yung hospitality sector who has greater expertise sa pangangalaga ng tao.

1389
01:24:55,420 --> 01:24:56,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Katulad nung nangyari po sa COVID.

1390
01:24:57,680 --> 01:25:06,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At hindi po kaya ng gobyerno na magtayo ng accommodation with let's say 1,000, 2,000, 10,000 rooms.

1391
01:25:06,780 --> 01:25:09,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Wala po yan sa linya ng trabaho ng gobyerno.

1392
01:25:09,520 --> 01:25:12,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: I think in the past, sinubukan na po yan, government-run hotels.

1393
01:25:12,580 --> 01:25:15,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At eventually, tinurn over din po sa private sector.

1394
01:25:16,020 --> 01:25:24,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, Mr. Senator, Mr. Chair, ay pwede naman po sa tingin ko, kasi ginawa na rin po ng OWA ito,

1395
01:25:24,680 --> 01:25:30,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: pwede naman po magpatakbo itong plano na rin ni Admin PY ito, ng smaller scale.

1396
01:25:30,940 --> 01:25:38,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So halimbawa, kung 50 rooms, 25 to 50 rooms, pansamantalang paglalagyan, pwede naman po yun.

1397
01:25:38,960 --> 01:25:43,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero on a bigger scale, sa tingin ko po, hindi kaya ng pamahalaan ito.

1398
01:25:43,360 --> 01:25:44,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: It's not sustainable.

1399
01:25:44,320 --> 01:26:01,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ang katapusan po niyan, Mr. Senator, Mr. Chair, ay magre-reklamo rin po yung mga tao na hindi nasa antas ng hospitality sector standards ang pangangalaga sa kanila.

1400
01:26:01,820 --> 01:26:08,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So sa tingin ko po, on a smaller scale, yes, pwede po hawakan ng DMW o ng OWA.

1401
01:26:08,320 --> 01:26:14,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero kung pangmalawa ka na po ito, sa tingin ko, the private sector is best suited.

1402
01:26:14,420 --> 01:26:15,360
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: to take care of them.

1403
01:26:15,420 --> 01:26:21,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kabayan Hotel, most notably, has been a foremost lodging space for them.

1404
01:26:22,160 --> 01:26:26,540
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Si Mr. Chair, narinig ko, nagtatanong siya, galing sa kanya itong katanungan.

1405
01:26:26,640 --> 01:26:26,960
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Ano na rin?

1406
01:26:29,720 --> 01:26:32,660
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Ano na rin nangyari dun sa kaso ng...

1407
01:26:32,660 --> 01:26:35,280
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Sa halfway house ni Mr. Ignacio.

1408
01:26:37,160 --> 01:26:39,900
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Naglabas po ang Ombudsman ng resolution.

1409
01:26:41,040 --> 01:26:44,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Una, recommending the filing of...

1410
01:26:44,320 --> 01:26:50,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Not recommending, but directing the filing of a case for usurpation of official functions.

1411
01:26:50,700 --> 01:26:56,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dahil pumirma po siya ng deed of sale na walang authority ng OWA Board of Trustees.

1412
01:26:57,740 --> 01:27:08,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: However, dinispis po yung aspeto ng plunder at saka Anti-Graft and Corrupt Practices Act.

1413
01:27:08,400 --> 01:27:09,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Na yun po ang minomotion.

1414
01:27:10,160 --> 01:27:13,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nag-file po kami motion for reconsideration.

1415
01:27:14,320 --> 01:27:17,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ako po mismo ang personal na nag-file nung motion na ito.

1416
01:27:17,220 --> 01:27:21,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi po, bahagi nung binili nila supposedly,

1417
01:27:22,040 --> 01:27:24,200
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: are condominium units.

1418
01:27:27,060 --> 01:27:27,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 52?

1419
01:27:27,740 --> 01:27:30,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 50 titles.

1420
01:27:30,800 --> 01:27:32,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Na nung nagkabayaran po,

1421
01:27:33,700 --> 01:27:38,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: strangely, giniba yung condominium na yun.

1422
01:27:38,700 --> 01:27:42,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Eh, ang problema, those titles were transferred to the government.

1423
01:27:43,200 --> 01:27:43,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, lumalabas.

1424
01:27:44,320 --> 01:27:48,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nag-ghost purchase po yung 52 condominium units.

1425
01:27:48,240 --> 01:27:51,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Mukhang hindi po na-pass upan yun ng Ubudzman sa resolution.

1426
01:27:52,840 --> 01:27:54,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Baka nakaligtaan lang.

1427
01:27:54,280 --> 01:27:57,000
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya sa motion for reconsideration namin, binabalikan po yun.

1428
01:27:57,080 --> 01:27:59,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi halagang 97 million pesos po yun.

1429
01:27:59,940 --> 01:28:03,300
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dagdag sa purchase price po na 97 million pesos yun.

1430
01:28:03,300 --> 01:28:09,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Na kung pupuntahan niyo yung lugar, wala po kayong makikitang condominium na nakatayo dun ngayon.

1431
01:28:09,200 --> 01:28:09,640
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Thank you.

1432
01:28:09,800 --> 01:28:14,100
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: At before I go, Mr. Chair, I'd like to reiterate again.

1433
01:28:14,320 --> 01:28:21,000
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: My full and firm support sa budget ng ating DMW at OWA at pagdating sa plenary sa budget.

1434
01:28:21,000 --> 01:28:29,480
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: I hope lahat ng mga kasamahan nating senador, especially you, na susuportahan itong dagdag budget.

1435
01:28:29,600 --> 01:28:34,420
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: Kahit man lang ito 2 billion, 2 billion sa DMW and 2 billion sa OWA.

1436
01:28:35,200 --> 01:28:36,760
Senator Raffy T. Tulfo: That's all, Mr. Chair. Thank you.

1437
01:28:36,800 --> 01:28:39,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you. Thank you very much, Senator Rafi Tulfo.

1438
01:28:39,800 --> 01:28:43,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: It would be a great help to this representation and to the...

1439
01:28:44,320 --> 01:28:49,100
Senator Joel Villanueva: ...the department of your help. Maraming salamat.

1440
01:28:49,960 --> 01:28:56,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: Let me, I don't know how to start, but let me, first things first, no? Siguro.

1441
01:28:57,500 --> 01:29:04,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Una, thank you for your update dun sa supposed to be halfway house, no?

1442
01:29:04,220 --> 01:29:09,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: That's, what is it called? Halfway house for OFWs? Ano bang tawag?

1443
01:29:09,000 --> 01:29:11,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yan po ang tawag niya dun. Yan po ang tawag niya.

1444
01:29:11,860 --> 01:29:14,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: And precisely...

1445
01:29:14,320 --> 01:29:19,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yung tanong ko ni Sen. Rafi, Chair Rafi, yan po ang isa sa mga pinagdibatihan namin noon.

1446
01:29:19,200 --> 01:29:25,400
