2016
02:01:59,000 --> 02:02:04,560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Different conflicts happening at the same time, pero lalo-lalo na sa Middle East.

2017
02:02:06,980 --> 02:02:14,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: May rest assured that during the Senate, marami naman tayong champion dito ng mga overseas Filipino workers natin in labor.

2018
02:02:15,100 --> 02:02:17,400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Senator Joel is one, Senator Bongo.

2019
02:02:17,740 --> 02:02:20,600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya mahal natin ang OFWs natin.

2020
02:02:20,780 --> 02:02:23,500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya na kahit na hindi na may iba doon, hindi kami mahal.

2021
02:02:23,500 --> 02:02:28,300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dahil, ewan ko lang bakit bali-mali yata yung nakakarating silang balita.

2022
02:02:28,500 --> 02:02:35,600
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero nakita nyo naman kami, trabaho lang dito, tanggalin natin yung politika kasi minsan ano nila yung politika lang.

2023
02:02:36,420 --> 02:02:37,540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tayo, trabaho lang.

2024
02:02:37,640 --> 02:02:46,240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And what's gonna be good for the majority, sa masakarami kung ano nakakabuti.

2025
02:02:47,580 --> 02:02:49,900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya yan, sabi ko nga, Senator Joel, thank you.

2026
02:02:52,140 --> 02:02:53,340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Magtutulong na lang kami para...

2027
02:02:53,500 --> 02:02:59,280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Lahat ng ano, mahirap man, masikip man yung ating, sabi ko nga, elbow room natin, gagawa natin ng paraan.

2028
02:02:59,920 --> 02:03:03,100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dahil hindi naman natin pwede pabayaan ng ating mga OFWs.

2029
02:03:03,500 --> 02:03:07,420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Na sila pong bumuhay ng ekonomiya natin for several decades.

2030
02:03:08,100 --> 02:03:08,320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Diba?

2031
02:03:08,980 --> 02:03:12,660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, kailangan sa oras ng kagipitan nila, eh, nandyan ho tayo.

2032
02:03:13,200 --> 02:03:14,880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro lang, misinformed lang sila.

2033
02:03:14,880 --> 02:03:22,120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sana lang malaman nila na yung ginagawa natin dito for healthcare, para sa kanilang welfare,

2034
02:03:22,120 --> 02:03:25,960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: lalo na sa universal healthcare, para sa kanilang mga pamilyang naiwan dito,

2035
02:03:26,680 --> 02:03:34,580
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ay inaayos natin para maramdaman at makagaan sa kanila rin pinapasan.

2036
02:03:34,940 --> 02:03:36,160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay? Thank you, Mr. Chair.

2037
02:03:36,580 --> 02:03:38,360
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you very much, Mr. Chairman.

2038
02:03:39,680 --> 02:03:43,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: Sige lang, okay lang pumalakpak. Okay lang. Para sa chairman natin.

2039
02:03:43,900 --> 02:03:49,560
Senator Joel Villanueva: No, no, no. Just to put on record, I am a living testimony of how Senator JV,

2040
02:03:49,560 --> 02:03:51,560
Senator Joel Villanueva: since he was a mayor of...

2041
02:03:52,120 --> 02:03:56,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: San Juan, kilala ko na siya, how he takes care of OFWs in San Juan and up to here.

2042
02:03:56,940 --> 02:04:07,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And we were together in so many, several times to go to different places from Hong Kong to Singapore to Europe, etc.

2043
02:04:07,460 --> 02:04:12,240
Senator Joel Villanueva: He's always been a avid supporter of our migrant workers.

2044
02:04:12,240 --> 02:04:21,160
Senator Joel Villanueva: Just to, ano lang, Senator JV, I mean, Chairman, like for example, a few days ago, we were tackling the budget of DFA.

2045
02:04:21,160 --> 02:04:26,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yung legal fund nila, there's 200 million, there's assistance to national, 1 billion.

2046
02:04:27,140 --> 02:04:31,320
Senator Joel Villanueva: And tingnan din natin yung utilization programs ng other agencies.

2047
02:04:31,640 --> 02:04:41,340
Senator Joel Villanueva: So, we'll do our part in looking for ways and means on how we can help look for the request of the budget of the Department of Migrant Workers and OFWs.

2048
02:04:41,400 --> 02:04:45,160
Senator Joel Villanueva: Again, Chairman JV, maraming salamat. Mabuhay ka. Thank you, thank you.

2049
02:04:45,160 --> 02:04:50,160
Senator Joel Villanueva: Okay. We will now give the floor to Senator Bong Go, who is also...

2050
02:04:51,160 --> 02:04:56,060
Senator Joel Villanueva: Equally, very passionate in fighting for our migrant workers.

2051
02:04:56,200 --> 02:04:57,540
Senator Joel Villanueva: Senator Bong Go, you have the floor, sir.

2052
02:04:57,760 --> 02:05:01,240
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chair, Senator Joel Villanueva.

2053
02:05:01,860 --> 02:05:05,760
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Unang-una, tamang-tama yung palakpak ninyo kasi siya yung chairman.

2054
02:05:05,760 --> 02:05:11,760
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So, kailangan talaga, netutulong yan si Senator JV.

2055
02:05:12,680 --> 02:05:14,820
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Lakasan nyo lang yung palakpak nyo pa next time.

2056
02:05:16,220 --> 02:05:18,340
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat po, Senator JV.

2057
02:05:18,620 --> 02:05:21,040
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Siya po yung finance chair po.

2058
02:05:21,160 --> 02:05:25,080
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Nang this year, sa Committee on Finance dito sa Senado.

2059
02:05:25,200 --> 02:05:30,700
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: And of course, our chairman po sa subcommittee, si Senator Joel Villanueva.

2060
02:05:31,340 --> 02:05:34,760
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Unang-una, ako po yung nagpapasalamat sa lahat po ng narito.

2061
02:05:35,180 --> 02:05:41,840
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Headed by Secretary Hans Kakdak, Administrator-Attorney Pai Kaunan.

2062
02:05:41,840 --> 02:05:50,680
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At sa lahat, Yusek Tutay, Yusek Olalia, Yusek Bay, Yusek Darlene Parito, Yusek Rasul,

2063
02:05:51,160 --> 02:06:03,240
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Yusek D. Guzman, lahat po ng COA, lahat ng nandito, Attorney Gapatan, Deputy Admin Susana Catapang,

2064
02:06:03,460 --> 02:06:11,800
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Deputy Admin Ryan, Vincent Uy, ED Victor Delisario, Dr. Servando Sergio.

2065
02:06:12,620 --> 02:06:13,600
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat sa inyo lahat.

2066
02:06:13,660 --> 02:06:21,140
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Unang-una, sa lahat ng nasa likod, maalala ko kayo, aside from the OFW na mga hero natin,

2067
02:06:21,160 --> 02:06:26,560
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: the modern day heroes natin, kayo rin po yung mga hero nung panahon ng pandemya.

2068
02:06:27,360 --> 02:06:32,300
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kayo po yung nag-aasikaso talaga, walang pahinga, 24 hours kayo on call.

2069
02:06:33,000 --> 02:06:43,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi pa po ito, Departamento, hindi pa ito, Department of Migrant Workers sa DOLEPA, DFA noon, POEA, OWA, at lahat po ng attached agencies.

2070
02:06:44,400 --> 02:06:45,660
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat po sa inyo.

2071
02:06:45,660 --> 02:06:50,660
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Doon ko nakita yung inyong dedikasyon sa pagtatrabaho.

2072
02:06:51,160 --> 02:06:56,060
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At napakahalaga po nitong Department of Migrant Workers.

2073
02:06:56,840 --> 02:07:06,420
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At kakagaling ko lang po ngayon sa Nagoya, sa Japan, para po sa Asian Games.

2074
02:07:06,700 --> 02:07:09,960
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sumuporta po tayo sa ating mga national athletes.

2075
02:07:10,220 --> 02:07:15,140
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Nag-cheer po tayo at makabigay mo lang ng moral support sa kanila.

2076
02:07:15,260 --> 02:07:17,500
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Congratulations po sa lahat ng ating mga athletes.

2077
02:07:17,640 --> 02:07:18,900
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Pagdasal po natin sila.

2078
02:07:20,360 --> 02:07:20,900
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: And napansin.

2079
02:07:21,160 --> 02:07:26,860
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Napansin ko, halos lahat ng pinupuntahan ko roon, thankful naman po sila.

2080
02:07:26,960 --> 02:07:29,680
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Nababanggit po ang inyong mga pangalan.

2081
02:07:30,200 --> 02:07:33,200
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Administrator Kaonan, in fact, galing daw po kayo doon.

2082
02:07:33,300 --> 02:07:40,820
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Meron kayong gathering among mga, anong gathering po yun?

2083
02:07:43,160 --> 02:07:44,600
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Yeah, just recently.

2084
02:07:44,880 --> 02:07:45,920
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Just recently, no.

2085
02:07:46,380 --> 02:07:49,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Nababanggit po kayo at talagang masaya naman po sila.

2086
02:07:49,440 --> 02:07:50,880
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kaya ako po, full support po.

2087
02:07:50,880 --> 02:07:56,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kaya ako po always sa budget ng Department of Migrant Workers.

2088
02:07:56,640 --> 02:07:57,680
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Yearly naman po yan.

2089
02:07:57,900 --> 02:08:02,700
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At alam nyo naman po na ipinaglaban po natin ito na may isa batas ito.

2090
02:08:02,800 --> 02:08:07,720
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Through the principal sponsor natin, si Senator Joel Villanueva.

2091
02:08:08,180 --> 02:08:09,660
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Noon na, hirap na hirap po kami nito.

2092
02:08:10,460 --> 02:08:15,040
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Walang may gusto na magkaroon ng sariling departamento.

2093
02:08:15,500 --> 02:08:19,320
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Remember, more than 10 million migrant workers.

2094
02:08:19,320 --> 02:08:20,320
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Wala man lang sariling departamento.

2095
02:08:20,880 --> 02:08:24,620
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: E yung iba nga, merong sariling departamento.

2096
02:08:24,840 --> 02:08:30,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Yung represent nila o kinikater nila, napakaliit lang po na portion ng population.

2097
02:08:30,620 --> 02:08:32,080
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ito pa, na more than 10 million.

2098
02:08:32,260 --> 02:08:33,260
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At napakahalaga po.

2099
02:08:33,400 --> 02:08:38,220
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Noon, wala pa itong DMW, yung mga kababayan natin,

2100
02:08:38,320 --> 02:08:42,860
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: nananawagan sa radyo, sa Facebook, sa telebisyon, kahit sino na lang po nilalapitan.

2101
02:08:43,340 --> 02:08:47,880
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ngayon po, nilagay na po sa isang departamento para sa ating mga migrant workers.

2102
02:08:47,880 --> 02:08:48,640
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat po.

2103
02:08:48,760 --> 02:08:50,300
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Naging batas po ito.

2104
02:08:50,300 --> 02:08:57,180
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So, Republic Act No. 11641, Principal Sponsor, Sen. Joel Villanueva, pinaglaban natin.

2105
02:08:57,320 --> 02:09:01,080
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At finally, naipasa po ito noong 18th Congress.

2106
02:09:01,500 --> 02:09:08,280
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At pangako po ito ni former President Duterte na maisa batas at meron ng sariling departamento na nakatutok.

2107
02:09:08,660 --> 02:09:13,100
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So, ngayon po, kaya ganoon na lang po akong ka-full support sa DMW.

2108
02:09:13,760 --> 02:09:18,000
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At yung pangarap natin noon ay isa katuparan po talaga.

2109
02:09:18,980 --> 02:09:20,100
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Napansin ko lang po ngayon.

2110
02:09:20,300 --> 02:09:30,020
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Speaking of the budget, napansin ko lang po sa proposed 2027 budget amounting to a 37.6 billion.

2111
02:09:30,020 --> 02:09:38,040
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: The DBM recommended only 11.6 billion, equivalent to 30.8 of the total amount requested.

2112
02:09:38,580 --> 02:09:46,180
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Among those not included in the NEP are additional funding for Action Fund and funding for the creation of new migrant workers offices.

2113
02:09:46,460 --> 02:09:50,140
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: We want to know how will this affect

2114
02:09:50,280 --> 02:09:52,580
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: the operations of DMW next year.

2115
02:09:53,120 --> 02:09:59,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mr. Chair, isa rin po sa ating sinusulong ang pagtatag ng OFW Hospital through Executive Order 154.

2116
02:10:00,100 --> 02:10:03,420
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Meron na po tayong OFW Hospital sa Pampanga.

2117
02:10:03,660 --> 02:10:07,720
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Nagtulungan po ang national government, local government, at private sector.

2118
02:10:07,840 --> 02:10:11,520
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Meron po magandang hospital doon, dedicated sa ating mga OFW.

2119
02:10:12,160 --> 02:10:20,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At this Congress, I also filed Senate Bill 414, institutionalizing the OFW Hospital.

2120
02:10:20,160 --> 02:10:23,700
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ano na po ang status ng OFW Hospital?

2121
02:10:23,940 --> 02:10:27,080
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dahil kayo po ang namamahala.

2122
02:10:27,240 --> 02:10:34,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi naman po ito na turnover sa DOH since under po ito ng Department of Migrant Workers.

2123
02:10:35,200 --> 02:10:38,420
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Magkano na po ba ang kailangan para sa operation ng hospital?

2124
02:10:38,660 --> 02:10:39,380
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kumusta na po?

2125
02:10:40,000 --> 02:10:46,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: How will the reduction in funding affect the hospital's operations and the delivery of services to our OFWs?

2126
02:10:46,920 --> 02:10:50,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mr. Chair, dapat po tuloy-tuloy ang suporta natin sa OFWs.

2127
02:10:50,460 --> 02:10:55,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dahil po para sa ating mga OFWs po ito at sa kanilang mga pamilya.

2128
02:10:56,360 --> 02:11:00,540
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Additionally, Mr. Chair, para mas maging accessible ang servisyong medikal sa OFWs,

2129
02:11:00,600 --> 02:11:06,740
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: nag-file din po tayo ng Senate Bill 1290 or ang proposed OFW Wards Act.

2130
02:11:07,340 --> 02:11:11,780
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi naman po lahat ng OFWs kayang pumunta po ng Pampanga para magpagamot doon.

2131
02:11:11,880 --> 02:11:19,180
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kaya nararapat lamang po na meron dedicated sa kanila na OFW Wards na available po sa iba't ibang parte ng bansa.

2132
02:11:19,180 --> 02:11:30,480
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Gusto ko lang po isingit, Mr. Chair, bagamat hindi po ito parte ng budget ng Department of Migrant Workers,

2133
02:11:30,680 --> 02:11:41,920
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: pero apektado po ang ating mga kababayan, mga OFWs, mostly mga OFWs dahil kailangan po nila ng passport pag nagbiyahe po sila.

2134
02:11:41,920 --> 02:11:46,540
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mr. Chair, during the last budget hearing of the Department of Foreign Affairs,

2135
02:11:46,840 --> 02:11:48,920
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: there was a discussion on the proposed income.

2136
02:11:49,180 --> 02:11:57,140
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Increase in the cost of Philippine passports, citing inflation, VAT, price increases, and significantly higher transportation costs.

2137
02:11:57,860 --> 02:12:01,740
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Nabanggit ko po ito dahil kakagaling ko lang po sa Nagoya, Japan.

2138
02:12:01,980 --> 02:12:09,380
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At isa rin po sa mga usap-usapan ng ating mga kababayan doon na may planong itaas nga po ang presyo ng passport application fee.

2139
02:12:09,380 --> 02:12:14,060
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At hindi lang po basta itataas.

2140
02:12:14,780 --> 02:12:17,460
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mataas po talaga yung dinagdag kung sasakali.

2141
02:12:19,180 --> 02:12:23,900
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Pagdoblihin mula 950 pesos, magiging 1,500 pesos.

2142
02:12:24,420 --> 02:12:29,880
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Huwag naman po, sana, nakikiusap po tayo sa Department of Foreign Affairs.

2143
02:12:30,020 --> 02:12:32,060
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Pakiusapan nyo naman po yung printing office.

2144
02:12:32,220 --> 02:12:33,540
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ito yung tinatawag na APO.

2145
02:12:34,220 --> 02:12:36,060
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sana po na huwag naman po.

2146
02:12:36,160 --> 02:12:37,520
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi po napapanahon sa ngayon.

2147
02:12:37,620 --> 02:12:39,060
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hira po ang ating mga kababayan.

2148
02:12:39,180 --> 02:12:40,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Nasa crisis po tayo.

2149
02:12:40,440 --> 02:12:46,280
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At bawat piso po, bawat sentimo na kinikita ng mga OFWs natin,

2150
02:12:46,720 --> 02:12:48,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: ay napakahalaga po yun na meron silang...

2151
02:12:49,180 --> 02:12:52,540
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: dadalhin sa kanilang mga pamilya.

2152
02:12:52,700 --> 02:12:54,900
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Bawat piso, importante po yun sa kanila.

2153
02:12:55,680 --> 02:12:58,480
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At yun po, naging reaction mga nakausap ko.

2154
02:12:58,640 --> 02:13:02,620
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kitang-kita nyo naman po ang lungkot sa mga kababayan nating OFWs.

2155
02:13:02,820 --> 02:13:05,300
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At yung iba po, medyo galit.

2156
02:13:05,460 --> 02:13:08,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sana naman po, huwag ito matuloy.

2157
02:13:10,020 --> 02:13:13,580
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sabi ko, wala bang katapusan ang pahirap sa ating mga kababayan?

2158
02:13:14,380 --> 02:13:16,500
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Para sa akin, hindi po ito katanggap-tanggap.

2159
02:13:16,640 --> 02:13:18,340
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Huwag naman po, muna sana.

2160
02:13:18,340 --> 02:13:21,340
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kung kaya naman po i-subsidize ng gobyerno,

2161
02:13:21,940 --> 02:13:26,800
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: kesa naman po masayang yung pondo sa korupsyon,

2162
02:13:26,920 --> 02:13:31,840
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: sana naman gamitin na lang po, maayos at i-subsidize na lang po dito

2163
02:13:31,840 --> 02:13:36,640
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: sa mga pangangailangan po ng ating mga kababayan OFWs.

2164
02:13:36,700 --> 02:13:38,940
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Huwag na sanang mag-increase sa ngayon.

2165
02:13:39,360 --> 02:13:41,460
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ramdam ko po ang sentimento ng ating mga kababayan.

2166
02:13:41,580 --> 02:13:43,840
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At alam ko rin po, ramdam nyo yan.

2167
02:13:43,840 --> 02:13:47,840
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dahil kayo po ang nag-aasikaso sa ating mga kababayan.

2168
02:13:48,340 --> 02:13:49,500
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kababayan OFWs.

2169
02:13:49,580 --> 02:13:51,580
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ramdam ko ang sentimento ng ating mga kababayan

2170
02:13:51,580 --> 02:13:54,780
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: sa gitna ng matinding krisis na pinagdadaanan ang taong bayan ngayon.

2171
02:13:55,380 --> 02:13:58,360
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Never ending na ba talaga ang dagdag pahirap sa mga Pilipino?

2172
02:13:58,940 --> 02:14:02,220
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ilagay po natin ang ating mga sarili sa sitwasyon ng ating OFWs

2173
02:14:02,220 --> 02:14:06,480
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: na araw-araw nagsasakripisyo po para sa kanilang pamilya at sa ating bayan.

2174
02:14:07,400 --> 02:14:12,300
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Tinitiis po nila yung lungkot na mapalayo sa kanilang mga pamilya.

2175
02:14:12,300 --> 02:14:16,960
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Alam ko, mas marami sa kanila na gusto pong umuwi dito sa ating bayan.

2176
02:14:17,040 --> 02:14:18,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dito na lang po manirahan.

2177
02:14:18,340 --> 02:14:20,420
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Pero kailangan po nila magtrabaho doon.

2178
02:14:21,280 --> 02:14:25,560
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Tandaan natin, isang beses lang tayo dadaan sa mundong ito, napakabilis po ng panahon.

2179
02:14:26,000 --> 02:14:31,540
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sana easy nila dito na manirahan sa ating bayan kaysa sa malayo sa kanilang pamilya.

2180
02:14:31,660 --> 02:14:33,000
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Pero tinitiis po nila yun.

2181
02:14:33,580 --> 02:14:36,480
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Tinitiis nila ang sakit na mapalayo sa kanilang mga mahal sa buhay.

2182
02:14:37,140 --> 02:14:41,320
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi pinapansin ang inip, gutom at pagod basta makapagtipid

2183
02:14:41,320 --> 02:14:45,960
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: at may padala ang pinaghirapang sahod para may panggastos po sa kanilang pamilya

2184
02:14:45,960 --> 02:14:48,320
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: at para rin manatiling buhay ang ating ekonomiya.

2185
02:14:48,340 --> 02:14:55,300
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Tapos ito po ang isusukli ng Estado sa kanila, dagdag na gastusin.

2186
02:14:56,240 --> 02:14:57,340
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi po dapat ito.

2187
02:15:00,000 --> 02:15:03,640
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dapat nga huwag nang dagdagan pa ang bigat na pasan ng ating mga kababayan.

2188
02:15:04,280 --> 02:15:10,080
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Imbis na humanap ang gobyerno ng paraan para matulungan sila at mapagaan kahit papanong buhay ng OFWs,

2189
02:15:10,460 --> 02:15:16,500
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: baliktad po ang nangyayari, nagiging paurong, problema at sakit ng ulo ang naghihintay sa kanila dito sa bansa.

2190
02:15:17,480 --> 02:15:21,360
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At also Mr. Chair, here is the ironic part.

2191
02:15:21,360 --> 02:15:31,840
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Noong panahon po ni dating Pangulong Rodrigo Duterte, ang dinoble natin noon noong panahon ni former President Duterte ay yung serbisyo.

2192
02:15:32,060 --> 02:15:36,000
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mula 5 years, ginawa pong 10 years ang validity ng Philippine Passport.

2193
02:15:36,460 --> 02:15:43,740
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Dinoble natin ang pakinabang para sa ating mga mamamayan.

2194
02:15:44,080 --> 02:15:50,740
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Million-million Pilipino ang nakinabang at natuwa dahil dito hindi na nila kailangan pumila pa dyan sa pag-renewal.

2195
02:15:51,360 --> 02:15:55,960
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mula 5 years, ginawa po ng kanilang passport. After 10 years na nila, kailangan pong mag-renew.

2196
02:15:56,840 --> 02:16:08,560
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sana po, may iwasan po ito ang pagtaas ng passport processing fee.

2197
02:16:08,560 --> 02:16:16,820
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ako po ay nakikiusap sa Department of Foreign Affairs at sa APO, sa Printing Office,

2198
02:16:17,760 --> 02:16:20,740
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: na sana naman po huwag munang taasan.

2199
02:16:21,360 --> 02:16:29,900
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ang passport processing fee dahil hirap po ang ating mga kababayan, lalong-lalo na po ang mga OFWs.

2200
02:16:30,720 --> 02:16:34,340
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ang kailangan ngayon, serbisyo, hindi po negosyo.

2201
02:16:35,360 --> 02:16:38,320
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At gusto ko lang po marinig yung position ninyo ukol dito.

2202
02:16:38,320 --> 02:16:47,600
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: And I'm sure sana tutulan nyo rin po ang pagtaas ng passport processing fee.

2203
02:16:48,000 --> 02:16:51,280
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: On another note po, Mr. Chair, Secretary.

2204
02:16:51,360 --> 02:16:59,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: During my recent visit sa Nagoya, nabanggit po ng Consulate Office o ng Congen doon,

2205
02:16:59,820 --> 02:17:05,880
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: si Consul General Sherlyn Manangkil na walang labor office or migrant workers office sa Nagoya.

2206
02:17:05,880 --> 02:17:12,680
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Despite the significant number of OFWs in the area, sana po matulungan ang DMW sa isyong ito

2207
02:17:12,680 --> 02:17:16,520
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: dahil importante po na may malalapitan ang ating mga OFWs sa ibang bansa.

2208
02:17:17,080 --> 02:17:19,640
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At ang Nagoya po ang pinakamaraming.

2209
02:17:21,360 --> 02:17:33,380
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Pilipino workers po dahil na doon po yung mga planta ng Toyota at mga iba pang mga malalaking kumpanya.

2210
02:17:33,760 --> 02:17:42,180
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So sila po ang pinakamaraming Pilipino migrant workers sa Japan, ang Nagoya po.

2211
02:17:42,280 --> 02:17:47,400
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sila po yung walang labor office or migrant workers office sa Nagoya.

2212
02:17:47,760 --> 02:17:51,020
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At hindi lang po sa Nagoya, sana po makapag-establish din tayo.

2213
02:17:51,360 --> 02:17:57,880
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sa mga bansa at lugar na maraming OFWs, dapat po magkaroon ng sapat at readily available na pondo

2214
02:17:57,880 --> 02:18:04,420
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: para sa ating mga OFWs na naiipit sa conflict areas, lalo na po sa gitna ng kaguluhan sa Middle East.

2215
02:18:04,420 --> 02:18:08,600
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ito mismo ang dahilan kung bakit napakalaga po nitong action fund.

2216
02:18:09,440 --> 02:18:14,800
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Mr. Chair, sana magawan mo ito ng paraan. Alam ko namang mag-a-action ka kagadyan.

2217
02:18:16,760 --> 02:18:20,060
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Unahin natin sila. Pagtutulungan po namin ito.

2218
02:18:21,360 --> 02:18:28,620
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Alang-alang na lang po. Isa-alang-alang natin ang kapakanan ng ating mga migrant workers, mga OFWs.

2219
02:18:29,160 --> 02:18:35,620
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kapag may digmaan o biglang krisis, hindi maaaring kulang ang pondo at hindi maaaring mabagal ang pagkilos ng gobyerno.

2220
02:18:36,080 --> 02:18:41,640
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kaya nakakabahala po na hindi maisama sa NEP ang additional funding requested for the action fund.

2221
02:18:41,640 --> 02:18:50,240
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: I hope that in considering the 2027 budget, we can ensure that the DMW has sufficient resources to respond immediately.

2222
02:18:51,360 --> 02:18:54,120
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Wherever and wherever our OFWs are in danger.

2223
02:18:54,120 --> 02:19:04,720
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Paalala ko lang po sa DMW at sa OWA. Lagi po natin unahin ang kapakanan ng ating mga OFWs dahil para po sa kanila ang lahat na may inisiyatibo na ginagawa natin dito.

2224
02:19:05,620 --> 02:19:21,120
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At ito yung parati kong pinapaalala sa lahat. Hindi lang po sa DMWs, sa DFA, sa mga ambasador during hearing po dito ng confirmation ng kanilang appointment or nomination.

2225
02:19:21,360 --> 02:19:35,440
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Nila sa mga career foreign service or sa mga ambasadors natin. And even during the time na kayo po kinonfirm namin dito, Secretary Kakdak, maalala nyo, sinabi ko lang po sa inyo,

2226
02:19:36,200 --> 02:19:48,600
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: bukas po ang ating opisina 24x7 para sa ating mga OFWs. Lalong-lalo na po sa panahon na kailangan nila ng tulong at saklolo. Yun lang po ang pakiusap ko sa inyo.

2227
02:19:49,240 --> 02:19:51,340
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Full support po ko always sa inyong...

2228
02:19:51,360 --> 02:20:02,660
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: ...departamento. Pagtutulungan po namin. Salamat sa inyong servisyo sa ating mga kababayan. You may answer na po sa mga tanong ko po.

2229
02:20:02,660 --> 02:20:19,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Maraming salamat, Mr. Chair, Senator Goh. Malaking bahagi po ng budget process. Ang madinig namin ang inyong words of encouragement at payo at katanungan na mataas po ang pagtanaw namin sa naging papel ninyo sa pagtalaga ng aming kagawaran.

2230
02:20:20,120 --> 02:20:21,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasama ng ating chair.

2231
02:20:21,360 --> 02:20:40,780
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ang era po of implementation ay dito na nga po sa panahon ng ating Pangulo, Mahal ng Pangulong Bongbong Marcos. Kaya't sa pag-implement po ng batas na itinalaga ninyo, tinatanggap po namin 101%, Mr. Senator, ang lahat ng inyong binanggit sa ngayon.

2232
02:20:41,260 --> 02:20:51,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Unahin ko po yung OFW Hospital kasi alam ko po napakalapit sa inyong puso. Ang OFW Hospital, malugod ko pong inuulat na 190,000 po.

2233
02:20:51,360 --> 02:21:03,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ang napaglingkuran na nating OFWs. Di lamang OFWs, Mr. Senator, dahil alam namin nung tinalaga ang ospital, inasasangalang-alang nyo rin ang nanay at tatay at mga anak na mga OFWs.

2234
02:21:03,220 --> 02:21:17,920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya't kung kayo po ay napunta doon, nadalaw doon, Mr. Senator, marami po mga lolo at lola bilang nanay at tatay na mga OFWs na pinaglilingkuran natin, mga bata, mga babies, mga teenagers na anak.

2235
02:21:18,640 --> 02:21:21,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At ang atin pong...

2236
02:21:21,360 --> 02:21:34,320
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: ...budget ay 300 million na ibinigay. Kaya't ang hinihiling po namin madagdagan. Sinaalang-alang pa rin namin ng OFW Hospital dito sa aming request for consideration for around 2 billion.

2237
02:21:34,980 --> 02:21:41,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasama na po yung Action Fund and around 200 million of the OFW Hospital, Mr. Senator.

2238
02:21:42,420 --> 02:21:49,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And marami na po tayong mga napaglingkuran, marami na po mga babies na ipinanganak sa hospital na ito.

2239
02:21:49,420 --> 02:22:01,700
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At sa liderato ni President Marcos, may Cancer Care Center na po tayong planong ilunsad next year. Dinagdaga na po ng Cancer Care Center ito, OFW Hospital.

2240
02:22:02,740 --> 02:22:19,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dito po sa ating Action Fund, without any question, ay talagang gusto po talaga natin, lalo papating ka rin po. Tama po yung sinabi ninyo na napakahalaga ng Action Fund, ang legal, medical, financial.

2241
02:22:19,420 --> 02:22:33,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Repatriation and other forms of analogous assistance na pondo natin. Higit kumulang, lagpas isandaang OFWs na po ang nakatanggap ng financial assistance sa Action Fund.

2242
02:22:34,160 --> 02:22:47,940
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Higit kumulang sa legal assistance ay mga 20,000 na mga OFWs na kinabang sa mga kasong hinahandle ng ating mga higit kumulang mga 100 lawyers worldwide.

2243
02:22:47,940 --> 02:23:04,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasi po mga law firms ang inahire natin, 25 law firms with at least 4 lawyers each. E mga 100 lawyers po yan under the Action Fund on average, dito sa ating, na tumutulong sa ating mga OFWs worldwide.

2244
02:23:05,880 --> 02:23:17,280
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: And kaya't 1 billion pong hinihiling namin, Mr. Senator, na karagdagang pondo. Kasi nga po, dito sa huling gera, nung Marso, Abril, Mayo,

2245
02:23:17,940 --> 02:23:32,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: 12,000 ang pa-uwi natin together with the OWA. At 20,000 naman, mga hindi na-uwi pero naapektuhan ng trabaho, binigyan natin ng financial assistance, basic needs, food, water, at other basic needs abroad.

2246
02:23:32,620 --> 02:23:39,800
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So marami po tayong natulungan sa panahon ng crisis. So yung crisis assistance, crisis response po natin, Mr. Senator.

2247
02:23:39,960 --> 02:23:47,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Rest assured, our people stand ready kung ano pong nagampana natin nung COVID at nung iba pang mga global crisis nung nakaraan.

2248
02:23:47,940 --> 02:23:56,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sa kasaysayan natin sa migration governance, ay handa pa rin ho kami. We're still the same, ready to serve, willing to serve.

2249
02:23:56,560 --> 02:24:08,760
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: We still have the brave and resilient core under the leadership of the President na nakatalaga sa ating Department of Migrant Workers, Overseas and Regional Personnel.

2250
02:24:08,760 --> 02:24:17,920
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pati po yung mga nanunumbalik na OFWs, Mr. Senator, tinutulungan po ng Action Fund. Yung mga distress po natin, yung mga seafarers na nahos,

2251
02:24:17,940 --> 02:24:27,080
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: pagbalik po nila, tinutulungan natin. Yung mga inapi ng kanilang mga employers sa abroad, pag-uwi, tinutulungan din po natin.

2252
02:24:27,200 --> 02:24:32,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yung mga pinapauwi sa deportation, na cruise ship sa US, tinutulungan po natin pag-uwi nila.

2253
02:24:33,160 --> 02:24:37,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Mga victims of illegal recruitment and human trafficking, tinutulungan din po natin.

2254
02:24:38,360 --> 02:24:46,560
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Panghuli po, sa pasaporte, kaysa niyo po kami. Sa amin po, napakahalaga ng inyong...

2255
02:24:47,940 --> 02:24:59,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Tinutulungan sa atin, yung inyong sinasabi sa atin na supportahan ang mga OFWs, napakahalaga din po ng posisyon ng ating mga OFWs dito.

2256
02:24:59,180 --> 02:25:09,600
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: In fact, pinakamahalaga ang kanilang saluubin, Mr. Senator. Kailangan ko rin pong kausapin ang ating mahal na Secretary of Foreign Affairs.

2257
02:25:09,860 --> 02:25:15,340
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: She is a co-equal, if not a primus inter pares sa gabinete, ang Secretary of Foreign Affairs.

2258
02:25:15,340 --> 02:25:22,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya't gagalangin din po natin ang kanilang findings dito sa kanilang pagtataas ng fees.

2259
02:25:23,260 --> 02:25:32,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Bagamat ganon, maintindihan din po naman ako ng ating SFA, I am sure, kapag naman nagdulog din ako o nag-feedback kung anong nasa saluubin ng ating mga OFWs.

2260
02:25:33,500 --> 02:25:35,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya't gagawin ko po ito, Mr. Senator.

2261
02:25:35,740 --> 02:25:44,880
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Malaking bagay po yun, Secretary Hans Kakdak, na mapakiusapan nyo yung counterpart nyo sa Department of...

2262
02:25:45,340 --> 02:25:49,640
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: ...Foreign Affairs, na mapakiusapan yung APO Production Unit, no?

2263
02:25:50,200 --> 02:25:53,140
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: May GOCC po ito, sila yung nagpiprint ng passport.

2264
02:25:53,380 --> 02:26:01,240
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sana po ipagpaliban muna yung pag-increase ng passport processing fee.

2265
02:26:01,240 --> 02:26:08,720
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kung maaari nga lang po, huwag lang itaas, babaan nyo pa yung presyo kung mas maaari.

2266
02:26:09,280 --> 02:26:14,680
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Malaking bagay po yun, malaking tulong yun sa ating mga kababayan, na bawat piso at bawat centimo,

2267
02:26:15,340 --> 02:26:16,780
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: talaga po sa ating mga OFWs.

2268
02:26:16,860 --> 02:26:27,460
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At naintindihan po yun ni Secretary Tess Lazaro dahil alam niya ang totoong sitwasyon ng...

2269
02:26:27,460 --> 02:26:32,600
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: ...kayo po ang nakakalam ng totoong sitwasyon ng ating mga migrant workers mga OFWs.

2270
02:26:32,640 --> 02:26:35,280
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat po sa inyong pagmamahal sa OFWs.

2271
02:26:35,520 --> 02:26:37,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Nakaligtaan ko lang, Mr. Senator, yung Senagoya.

2272
02:26:38,840 --> 02:26:43,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasama po kami ni Admin Piwai nung presidential trip sa Japan.

2273
02:26:44,180 --> 02:26:45,220
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At doon nga po nagkakataon.

2274
02:26:45,340 --> 02:26:48,840
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kakausap din kami ni Congen Manangkil.

2275
02:26:50,100 --> 02:26:57,020
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At siyempre, inatasan din po tayo ng ating Pangulo na natignan kung saan pa natin mapapalaganap ang ating presensya.

2276
02:26:57,140 --> 02:26:58,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kasama na rin po si Sec. Tess Lazaro.

2277
02:26:59,480 --> 02:27:01,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: At meron na po kaming understanding.

2278
02:27:01,920 --> 02:27:04,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Agree po kami na kailangan magtama po kayo.

2279
02:27:04,620 --> 02:27:08,500
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ayon sa datos, maraming OFWs, mas maraming OFWs sa Nagoya.

2280
02:27:09,080 --> 02:27:14,980
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Kaya po, agree po kami at magtatalaga po tayo ng Migrant Workers Office doon, Mr. Senator.

2281
02:27:15,340 --> 02:27:17,040
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ikinig po kami sa inyong iminungkahi.

2282
02:27:18,180 --> 02:27:20,580
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Maraming salamat po sa pagkonsidera.

2283
02:27:21,100 --> 02:27:27,240
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At tamang-tama po kanina, nandito nga si ating chairperson ng Senate Committee on Finance.

2284
02:27:27,500 --> 02:27:28,940
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Malaking bagay po yun dahil.

2285
02:27:30,060 --> 02:27:36,160
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At nandirito rin po ang ating subcom chairperson, Sen. Joel Villanueva, na pagtutulungan po namin.

2286
02:27:37,180 --> 02:27:42,940
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Sila po yung matagal na nakakaalam sa pangangailangan ng budget.

2287
02:27:43,640 --> 02:27:44,920
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi pa ito DMW.

2288
02:27:45,340 --> 02:27:47,680
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ang budget para sa ating OFWs.

2289
02:27:47,760 --> 02:27:55,080
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: And of course, tamang-tama rin dahil sa magkabilang lamesa, nandiyan ang administrator ng OWA.

2290
02:27:55,680 --> 02:28:00,580
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: May taga-remind rin po kay Sen. Joel, ang ating chairperson ng subcommittee.

2291
02:28:01,180 --> 02:28:04,020
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Kasi yung kapatid niya, nasa kabilang lamesa rin po.

2292
02:28:06,180 --> 02:28:11,220
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Magkapatid po yan sila, administrator kaunan.

2293
02:28:11,940 --> 02:28:13,740
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: So, ma'am ha, huwag niyong kalimutan.

2294
02:28:13,740 --> 02:28:14,540
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Tamang-tama yan.

2295
02:28:14,600 --> 02:28:15,280
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Di malilimutan.

2296
02:28:15,340 --> 02:28:16,100
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Di malilimutan ni Sen. Joel.

2297
02:28:16,440 --> 02:28:18,980
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Marami pong magre-remind.

2298
02:28:20,520 --> 02:28:26,920
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Tamang-tama yung pag-budget sponsor mo dito, Sen. Boss, Chairman.

2299
02:28:28,100 --> 02:28:29,260
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Yun lamang po.

2300
02:28:31,360 --> 02:28:32,600
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Yun lamang po.

2301
02:28:34,680 --> 02:28:37,460
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Anything po para sa ating OFWs.

2302
02:28:37,560 --> 02:28:40,360
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Ako naman po'y sumusuporta always.

2303
02:28:40,360 --> 02:28:45,200
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Hindi po ako mangangako na kayang maibigay lahat dito yan.

2304
02:28:45,340 --> 02:28:45,780
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Senado.

2305
02:28:45,920 --> 02:28:50,540
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Pero ipaglalaban po namin parati ang kapakanan ng ating mga OFWs.

2306
02:28:50,960 --> 02:28:53,140
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat po, Mr. Chair.

2307
02:28:53,320 --> 02:28:53,820
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Salamat po.

2308
02:28:54,780 --> 02:28:56,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Sen. Bong Go.

2309
02:28:56,680 --> 02:29:01,160
Senator Joel Villanueva: Has been with us since day one.

2310
02:29:01,160 --> 02:29:13,140
Senator Joel Villanueva: I still remember those days na I think we were able to tackle the bill on establishing the Department of Migrant Workers for almost two years, if I'm not mistaken.

2311
02:29:13,380 --> 02:29:15,260
Senator Joel Villanueva: And every time magkakaroon.

2312
02:29:15,340 --> 02:29:28,140
Senator Joel Villanueva: And every time magkakaroon ng mga roadblocks, pitstops, etc., si Sen. Bong Go yung pinaka talagang most dependable individual na kausap ko noon para i-push yung bill.

2313
02:29:28,480 --> 02:29:31,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: And true enough, naging batas po ito.

2314
02:29:31,500 --> 02:29:42,420
Senator Joel Villanueva: So we really put it into the records of this hall na malaking tulong yung ginawa ni Sen. Bong Go to establish the Department of Migrant Workers.

2315
02:29:42,420 --> 02:29:44,320
Senator Joel Villanueva: So again, thank you, Sen. Bong Go.

2316
02:29:45,340 --> 02:29:54,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: Especially now na nandyan na, hindi mo pa rin iniiwan at sumusuport pa rin sa budgetary requirements and requests ng DMW.

2317
02:29:54,340 --> 02:29:55,320
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you, Sen. Bong Go.

2318
02:29:55,320 --> 02:29:58,320
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: May I add something?

2319
02:30:00,000 --> 02:30:24,540
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: Alam niyo, nung panahon si Senator Joel, siya yung chairperson ng Labor Committee dito sa Senado. Muntik na siyang nawala ng pag-asa pero hindi po siya bumigay. Talagang pinaglaban niya. Sabi ko, boss, alang-alang na lang sa OFWs na, mga kababayan nating OFWs, please lang, huwag kang bumigay, paglaban mo pa rin, huwag kang mawala ng pag-asa.

2320
02:30:24,540 --> 02:30:37,060
Senator Christopher Lawrence T. Go: At true enough, yung ating panaginip nagkatotoo po na nagkaroon ng Department of Migrant Workers. Salamat sa iyong pagmamahal sa ating mga OFWs, Senator Joel Villanueva. Maraming salamat po.

2321
02:30:37,060 --> 02:30:54,060
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you again, Senator Bong. And let me stem my next questions dun sa binabanggit ka rin ni Senator Bong. Una yung sa Passport Act. I'm one of the authors of the 10 years validity of passports.

2322
02:30:54,540 --> 02:31:07,300
Senator Joel Villanueva: And yung APO publishing is under OP now. Is that correct? It's under OP now. Before, it's under BSP. So right now, if I'm not mistaken, it's under OP.

2323
02:31:07,300 --> 02:31:24,480
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I heard Secretary Tess Lazaro saying that she was able to talk to APO and nag-request na po sila. It's just that siguro concerted efforts, lahat tayo, magpagtalong-talungan po natin.

2324
02:31:24,540 --> 02:31:51,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Hindi maganda, especially right now, na itaas yung... And I'm with Senator Bong on this particular issue. Now, let me continue my questions with the Action Fund. Kasi tinitignan ko rin. Yung sa DFA, binanggit ko, yung legal fund nila is 200 million. Still there. Meron pa silang 1 billion na assistance to national. I'm not trying to get funding from DFA.

2325
02:31:51,120 --> 02:31:54,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: But in all honesty, when I...

2326
02:31:54,540 --> 02:32:15,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: I asked that question as to the utilization ng department, I think mataas pa rin yung available funds nila dito. I just don't know kung ngayong time of the year ba talagang ganon. I missed the budget briefing last time.

2327
02:32:15,000 --> 02:32:24,000
Senator Joel Villanueva: But if you look at the Action Fund, Secretary and the Admin Kaunan, pareho yung...

2328
02:32:24,540 --> 02:32:35,540
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yung Action Fund, merong repatriation, meron din ang OWA. Pati yung Action Fund, ang dami. May legal, may medical, repatriation. Merong...

2329
02:32:35,540 --> 02:32:50,660
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yun nga kanina binabanggit ni Sec Hans, yung mga distressed OFWs, yung may kailangan ng tulong because they were victimized by illegal recruitment, etc.

2330
02:32:50,660 --> 02:32:52,660
Senator Joel Villanueva: And then you have...

2331
02:32:54,540 --> 02:32:57,480
Senator Joel Villanueva: Reintegration, nandyan din po, nakaladge.

2332
02:32:57,480 --> 02:33:13,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: Now, looking at dun sa repatriation, hindi ko ba pag may nirepatriate tayo, of course, inuuna natin kaagad dyan dahil emergency yan eh. Most urgent yan na kailangang tulungan.

2333
02:33:13,220 --> 02:33:21,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: But the companies, the employers, they are also somehow liable in...

2334
02:33:21,220 --> 02:33:22,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: In...

2335
02:33:22,220 --> 02:33:23,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: For instance...

2336
02:33:24,540 --> 02:33:33,620
Senator Joel Villanueva: Giving help dun sa medical assistance, dun po sa pagbili, for example, ng tickets, plane tickets, etc.

2337
02:33:34,200 --> 02:33:44,280
Senator Joel Villanueva: May po ba tayong kaukulang pondo na nakukuha pa from their end, yung reimbursement na nakukuha?

2338
02:33:44,280 --> 02:33:53,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And at the same time, gaano po ang percentage-wise na nakaka-comply dito ng mga kumpanya?

2339
02:33:53,660 --> 02:33:54,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Or...

2340
02:33:54,540 --> 02:33:58,520
Senator Joel Villanueva: Or employers na nakukuha pa po natin?

2341
02:33:58,740 --> 02:33:59,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: Secretary?

2342
02:34:00,180 --> 02:34:03,060
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Tama po kayo, Mr. Senator.

2343
02:34:03,900 --> 02:34:10,820
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: The main responsibility to repatriate is with the employer and the mining agency.

2344
02:34:11,160 --> 02:34:17,680
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: For those who are still covered by their first two years contracts, kusa nandun pa yung agency.

2345
02:34:18,740 --> 02:34:24,180
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: But we're fully aware that most of OFWs, around 70% of OFWs,

2346
02:34:24,540 --> 02:34:27,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: are tinatawag na balik manggagawa.

2347
02:34:27,340 --> 02:34:34,740
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ibig sabihin, more than two years na sila sa abroad, at wala na silang agency covered under the compulsory insurance laws,

2348
02:34:35,140 --> 02:34:46,140
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: where repatriation will be covered by insurance company policy provided by the insurance company to the agency as the policyholder.

2349
02:34:47,680 --> 02:34:52,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ngayon, ang OWA po ang may mechanism doon ng reimbursement mechanism.

2350
02:34:52,260 --> 02:34:53,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, si...

2351
02:34:54,540 --> 02:34:57,260
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Admin PY, baka may kaukulang ulat po sa refunding.

2352
02:34:57,720 --> 02:35:04,160
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pero, in general, pag-crisis ang sitwasyon, we don't pause to say,

2353
02:35:04,600 --> 02:35:07,660
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: hindi kami yan, agency yan, etc.

2354
02:35:07,960 --> 02:35:10,880
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, tama po kayo, refund ang mekanismo natin.

2355
02:35:11,240 --> 02:35:16,440
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Ngayon, doon po sa medical, tama po kayo, many OFWs,

2356
02:35:16,860 --> 02:35:23,100
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: whether balik manggagawa or baguhan na OFWs, may insurance naman po sa host country, in general.

2357
02:35:23,340 --> 02:35:24,460
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, sa kanina,

2358
02:35:24,540 --> 02:35:28,940
Senator Joel Villanueva: binanggit nyo, just for me, my personal education, two years lang po yung compulsory.

2359
02:35:29,060 --> 02:35:30,580
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: For repatriation, yes.

2360
02:35:30,580 --> 02:35:31,800
Senator Joel Villanueva: For repatriation, two years.

2361
02:35:31,820 --> 02:35:32,420
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Yes, two years.

2362
02:35:32,420 --> 02:35:34,600
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pero sa medical, whether balik manggagawa...

2363
02:35:34,600 --> 02:35:39,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Sa medical, as long as they're covered by the medical insurance laws, regulations in the host country,

2364
02:35:39,580 --> 02:35:41,860
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: and in general, they are all, they are covered.

2365
02:35:42,680 --> 02:35:45,380
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, inuuna po natin munang i-avail nila.

2366
02:35:45,500 --> 02:35:50,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Habang may na-hospital ng OFW, hindi po natin agad sinasagot sa abroad yung hospital bills.

2367
02:35:50,640 --> 02:35:53,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Dahil malamang sa malamang, covered siya ng insurance doon.

2368
02:35:53,920 --> 02:35:54,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So,

2369
02:35:54,540 --> 02:35:59,120
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, tine-exhaust po muna yung insurance policy coverage.

2370
02:35:59,640 --> 02:36:05,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Pag nagkulang na po, o di kaya undocumented, kung saan walang insurance, doon po tayo pumapasok.

2371
02:36:05,860 --> 02:36:14,240
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: So, rest assured, hindi po tayo pumapasok agad kung covered naman ng insurance yung kababayan natin, hinahayaan muna natin.

2372
02:36:15,180 --> 02:36:21,400
DMW Secretary Hans Leo J. Cacdac: Doon po sa matter on the other matters like refund, baka si admin PY pumakapasok.

2373
02:36:21,400 --> 02:36:22,060
Senator Joel Villanueva: Yes, admin PY.

2374
02:36:22,200 --> 02:36:24,400
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I ask this question because I wanted to make sure...

2375
02:36:24,540 --> 02:36:29,400
Senator Joel Villanueva: I'm sure na yung mining agencies are also doing their share, doing their part.

2376
02:36:29,580 --> 02:36:34,180
Senator Joel Villanueva: And I wanted to understand where it goes, yung reimbursement, etc.

2377
02:36:34,400 --> 02:36:37,220
Senator Joel Villanueva: Saan napupunta? Inaano ba natin yun?

2378
02:36:38,520 --> 02:36:47,140
Senator Joel Villanueva: Dinapalik sa treasury or pwede rin natin gamitin na pondo para ipanggamit ng OWA?

2379
02:36:47,500 --> 02:36:48,140
Senator Joel Villanueva: Ma'am?

2380
02:36:48,500 --> 02:36:52,560
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Thank you very much, Chair, doon po sa tanong na yan.

2381
02:36:53,220 --> 02:36:54,500
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Una-una po, simulan ko.

2382
02:36:54,540 --> 02:37:00,560
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Doon sa RA 8042, Section 15, yan ang Emergency Repatriation Fund.

2383
02:37:00,980 --> 02:37:11,800
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Nandyan mismo nakasaad na ang may primary responsibility po patungkol sa repatriation ay yung mga employers po or yung kanila pong mga recruitment agencies.

2384
02:37:12,860 --> 02:37:22,540
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pero nasabi nga po na aming kalihim, pag emergency po, alam naman kung antahin pa natin sila na umakto, kaya po meron pong way of reimbursement.

2385
02:37:22,540 --> 02:37:23,580
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Okay.

2386
02:37:24,540 --> 02:37:30,180
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Mr. Chair, ako na hong unang aamin na medyo mahirap kolektahin.

2387
02:37:30,820 --> 02:37:45,460
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Kami po ay nagpapadala ng mga demand letter, nakailan na rin po kaming referral sa Department of Migrant Workers for proper administrative sanction, if that is kung hindi pa rin po sila magko-comply.

2388
02:37:45,460 --> 02:37:48,840
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pero over the years po, yun po ang nagiging proseso.

2389
02:37:49,380 --> 02:37:53,460
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Merong mga, meron pong ang OWA po ang nangungunang...

2390
02:37:54,540 --> 02:38:02,240
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: ...mag-gumastos para sa emergency repatriation, lalong-lalo na po, yung nasabi nga po ni SecHands, yung mga newly hired.

2391
02:38:02,860 --> 02:38:16,800
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: At pagkatapos po niyan ay we send the demand letter and then kung hindi pa rin po talaga sumagot, we refer to the, then po, POEA now, the Department of Migrant Workers.

2392
02:38:17,400 --> 02:38:23,580
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Opo, kasi po sila po ang regulatory, sila po may regulatory function.

2393
02:38:24,540 --> 02:38:37,700
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pero po, tama po yun, malaking porsyento po kasi nang tinutulungan natin ay mga balik manggagawa na o wala na pong recruitment agency.

2394
02:38:38,920 --> 02:38:49,700
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Mapayagan niya rin po akong sabihin and put on record, pag tinignan po namin, binalangkas po namin yung emergency repatriation fund at mas malaki po ang porsyento.

2395
02:38:50,580 --> 02:38:53,700
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Actually, Mr. Chair, mga lalampas siguro ng 90%.

2396
02:38:54,540 --> 02:39:03,880
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Kung titignan mo yung tulong pagtutungkol sa airfare, transportation, and shelter, ay land-based OFWs.

2397
02:39:03,880 --> 02:39:24,300
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ibig sabihin po, Mr. Chair, patungkol sa sea-based, ang mga manning agencies na ayon naman yan sa maritime convention at sa kanilang kontrata ay sumusunod at nagbibigay po at umaako nitong kanilang obligasyon under contract and under international maritime convention po.

2398
02:39:24,540 --> 02:39:32,480
Senator Joel Villanueva: Just to understand, Admin, pag naka-collect, what do you do with the collection?

2399
02:39:33,660 --> 02:39:38,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pwede bang gamitin ito ng OWA or ito'y binabalik sa treasury?

2400
02:39:38,620 --> 02:39:45,220
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Binabalik po natin sa treasury pag emergency repatriation fund po dahil ito po ay gaa.

2401
02:39:45,660 --> 02:39:50,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: And can you give us a ballpark figure like sample last year?

2402
02:39:51,540 --> 02:39:53,100
Senator Joel Villanueva: How much are we talking about here?

2403
02:39:54,540 --> 02:39:58,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: You were able to collect, which of course you made mention, very difficult.

2404
02:39:58,120 --> 02:40:09,720
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Very difficult, but for this year alone, Mr. Chair, over 10 million pa lang ang nakokolekta po namin na kumbaga naibalik sa treasury.

2405
02:40:09,820 --> 02:40:22,120
Senator Joel Villanueva: Pero yung demand letter and yun nga nasa kapending, meron kayong ballpark figure din kung magkano yung… kahit pa submit nyo na lang, just for our…

2406
02:40:22,660 --> 02:40:23,620
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Yes, Mr. Chair.

2407
02:40:23,620 --> 02:40:24,380
Senator Joel Villanueva: Just to make sure.

2408
02:40:24,540 --> 02:40:25,260
Senator Joel Villanueva: We understand.

2409
02:40:26,380 --> 02:40:27,460
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Opo, Mr. Chair.

2410
02:40:28,060 --> 02:40:35,880
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pero hindi ko po masasabi ngayon on record at magsasumiti na lang po kami sa komite patungkol sa actual amount.

2411
02:40:36,600 --> 02:40:44,960
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Pero ipauna ko na rin po, Mr. Chair, ang hinahabolan po namin ay 176 Philippine recruitment agencies.

2412
02:40:45,220 --> 02:40:47,120
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: Ang bayad pa lang po ay 13.

2413
02:40:47,760 --> 02:40:53,360
OWWA Administrator Patricia Yvonne "PY" M. Caunan: So yun po ay we will submit to the committee a more comprehensive report on this, Mr. Chair.

2414
02:40:53,480 --> 02:40:53,840
Senator Joel Villanueva: Thank you.

2415
02:40:54,040 --> 02:40:54,460
Senator Joel Villanueva: Appreciate it.

2416
02:40:54,540 --> 02:41:06,920
Senator Joel Villanueva: Let me go to another point dito sa part ng ating emergency protection ng ating mga kababayan.

2417
02:41:08,420 --> 02:41:18,940
Senator Joel Villanueva: May we know right now how many OFWs remain in conflict affected or yung nasa kategory ng high risk areas?

2418
02:41:18,940 --> 02:41:24,480
Senator Joel Villanueva: And of course, what level of contingency capacity

2419
02:41:24,540 --> 02:41:29,820
Senator Joel Villanueva: is required for their possible evacuation or repatriation?

2420
02:41:31,000 --> 02:41:33,800
Senator Joel Villanueva: Just to have an idea, Secretary?

2421
02:41:34,040 --> 02:41:46,560
